I've only ascended a couple of times so this is still brag-worthy to
me :p

My favourite character to play: female elf wizard. Female because,
well, I like having boobs :p

It took me a lot of runs in my recent bout of addiction with Nethack
to get to this one. A while back I got a character past the early
game, only to die in the plane of fire (despite a stash of amulets of
life saving) because I didn't know lava, you know, killed you.

I went down to Sokoban (without doing it) and then cleared out the
mines.

I was lucky enough to get an early wish in minetown, which is what
saved this game. I wished for what is now my staple early wish: an
amulet of life saving. I'm a careless player, so I need them.

At one point I used "Charm Monster" on a nymph to avoid it stealing
from me. I then used a polymorph trap to turn it into a minotaur,
which was a great help. He helpfully killed all the shopkeepers in the
entire dungeon for me, and I used the gold to get protection.

Not long after I died from a polymorphed soldier (still in the mines).
It had turned into an Angel, and I was stuck for an escape route. My
pet minotaur wasn't helping.

From that averted YASD things went well. (Mostly). Frustrated from
previous failed games, I decided to use incubi to raise my level.
After a few boring hours (hours? well it felt like that) chasing sex
demons I was overpowered enough to take on the rest of the dungeon
easily.

My minotaur died and I wasn't sorry, it was too much maintainence
feeding it while I was trying to have lots of hot demon sex.

I went straight down to the castle, clearing out all the levels, and
got my wand of wishing and another amulet of life saving. I breathed a
sigh of relief. I wouldn't die again this game, hopefully.

(Speaking of YASDs I once accidentally ate one of my own cockatrice
eggs. I typed fast, and pressed e + (egg) rather than w + (egg). I had
intended to use it to kill an annoying mind flayer).

So, from there I relaxed a bit and set about assembling my ascention
kit.

As for the other things I wished for:

I got the Master Key of Thievery. My strategy in this game was to
avoid artifacts, even Magicbane, so that I could artifact wish
effectively. I was using a highly enchanted staff as a weapon until
late in the game.

The rest of my wishes were mostly used on magic markers. I wrote a
spellbook of identify (took two tries) and then identified all my
gems. Then I found a unicorn, maxed out my luck, and started writing
spellbooks and scrolls.

I got a spellbook of polymorph and went around polypiling stuff.
Eventually I got all my ascension kit armor (boots of speeed,
gauntlets of power, etc), plus rings and later extra amulets of life
saving, from polymorphs and saved myself some wishes.

I took on the quest and Sokoban easily. I normally don't play Sokoban
but I needed the bag of holding.

At one point in all this I evaporated my cloak of magic restistance by
trying to fix its erosion. I thought I was confused when I was reading
that scroll, I wasn't, so yeah. I went up to where there was a priest,
stoned him, and took his robe. It was actually quite a good deal,
because with The Eye of A. and Magicbane as a backup I got plenty of
magic resistence, and the robe cancelled out the effects of those
gauntlets of power. It was nice to see all those 0% spell failure
rates :)

I also polymorphed myself into a cockatrice to make a load of egg
bombs, which came in handy later. I used a polymorph spell to turn
back, which made me "a new elf!" who happened to be male. Not liking
this, I eventually used an amulet of change to turn me back (once I
had polypiled for enough "oLS).

I accidentally evaporated my speed boots XD and after much polypiling
couldn't find any more, so I used my last wish on some new ones. I
also accidentally cancelled my whole inventory XD and accidentally let
a disenchanter remove all the enchantment on my hawaiian shirt XD This
was a clumsy game. Still, I got all my armor up to full enchantment
again eventually. I ditched my now +0 staff and started using a +2
Magicbane.

As a final preparation for the end game, I prayed and got crowned,
taking a spellbook of finger of death for my own.

The rest was quite easy. I killed the Wizard with a finger of death
before he woke up, and level teleported to the bottom level.

After recharging the bell of Opening twice, I opened the gate to the
sanctum and level teleported in - right next to the temple! It was
quite an easy steal with the finger of death at my disposal. I used a
cursed potion of gain level to get out, and raced for the first level
from there.

The planes were a breeze - THIS TIME - and the Astral was even more
so. I genocided all the monsters on the level that I could genocide,
skipped over famine's corpse (someone else had killed him), and it
just so happened that the first altar was mine. (And no, I didn't
cheat with a helm of opposite alignment, it doesn't seem in
character).

